# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Third-party source read for comparison. Never belongs in this repository —
# it is someone else's code, and its presence invites commits that describe
# this project in terms of theirs.
reference/
**/reference/

# Internal design notes, release plans and anything else not meant to ship with
# the source. Keep it here rather than scattering ignore rules by filename —
# a path says "this is not shared", a `*.md` rule only says "this is markdown".
design/

# Not part of the distributed source, for two different reasons.
#
# `planning/` is code no binary can reach -- 31 modules and the examples that went with them.
# It is kept because the ideas are worth keeping, but shipping 30,000 lines of unreachable
# code invites a reader to judge the product by it. Its own README explains the rule, and
# that README is what stays behind in this working copy.
#
# `TODO.md` is the competitive algorithm roadmap: what is not built yet, ranked, with the
# systems it is aimed at named. That is a plan, not a description of the software.
vectordb/planning/
vectordb/TODO.md

# Agent working instructions. They stay at their paths so Claude Code still loads them
# in this checkout, but they are candid about what is not wired up yet and are not shared.
CLAUDE.md

# Per-checkout agent settings. Local to whoever is working here, never shared.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Stray run output. `vectordb/.gitignore` has had this since the start; the repository root
# did not, which is how an empty `logs/vectordb_bench.log` came to be committed here.
logs/
